and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.lemma-b.1"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.lemma-b.1"],"id":"euler.lemma-b.1","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma B.1","locator":"Lemma B.1, Section B","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma B.1.** $S_\\Lambda$ commutes with derivatives, preserves parity and divergence freeness, and maps into fields supported on frequencies at most $2\\Lambda$. Its operator norms on $L^\\infty$ and on $C^{0,1/2}$ are bounded in terms of $\\psi$ alone. For every integer $m\\ge0$ and every normed-space-valued $f$ supported on frequencies at most $4\\Lambda$, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\sum_{|\\beta|=m}\\left\\lVert\\partial^\\beta f\\right\\rVert_\\infty\\le C_m\\Lambda^m\\left\\lVert f\\right\\rVert_\\infty . \\tag{B.1}\n\\end{equation}$$ For all integers $0\\le s\\le M$ and every $f\\in C^{M,1/2}$, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left\\lVert(\\operatorname{Id}-S_\\Lambda)f\\right\\rVert_{C^{s,1/2}}\n \\le C_M\\Lambda^{s-M}\\left\\lVert f\\right\\rVert_{C^{M,1/2}}. \\tag{B.2}\n\\end{equation}$$ The constants $C_m$ and $C_M$ depend only on their index and on $\\psi$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-b.1","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-5.9","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.9%22%2C%22euler.lemma-b.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.9%22%2C%22euler.lemma-b.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-b.1"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/node